  "description": "MAJDUB crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H144 Gd6 N6 O42 S6,6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.806-3.856 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 109.14-112.04°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C96H164Gd6N6O52S6.",
